From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Mendyka <jkmendyka@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 05:45:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] exynos-cpupm: port the 5.15 driver for the rev2 EL3 and
 APM firmware

The EL3 and APM firmware of bootloader rev2 (R870XXS2JZG3) were built
for the 5.15 kernel. EL3 runs no CPU power-off sequence until the kernel
sends SMC_CMD_CPUPM_ENABLE (0x82000008), which 5.15 does at the end of
the exynos-cpupm probe and 4.19 never did: every C2 entry failed, PSCI
CPU_OFF returned without powering the core down, and the SoC could not
reach system sleep with the second core online.

The 5.15 exynos-cpupm driver is adapted to 4.19:
- power modes selected by cal-id, never ORed into the PSCI state (always
  0x00010000); SICD with the 5.15 wakeup masks (WAKEUP_STAT cleared
  first), acpm_noti_dsu_cpd() and the 40 s deferred enabling; the
  hotplug flag that keeps a dying core out of C2;
- the vendor hooks android_vh_cpu_idle_enter/exit become
  exynos_cpupm_idle_enter/exit(), called by cpuidle-exynos64 in the 5.15
  order (PMUCAL and power modes before cpu_pm_enter(), cpu_pm_exit()
  before leaving them);
- SMC_CMD_CPUPM_ENABLE at the end of probe, with cpuidle paused around
  it; its state is in /sys/module/exynos_cpupm/parameters/el3_enable;
- the 4.19 API used by other drivers (idle-ip, exynos_cpu_pm_enter/exit,
  exynos_cpuhp_last_cpu, /sys/power/cpupm, the JIG block) is kept.

acpm_noti_dsu_cpd() in exynos-flexpmu-dbg was an empty stub and now
writes the flag to APM SRAM as in 5.15. cpuidle_profile_group_idle_register()
loses __init, since probe calls it. The driver needs the exynos-cpupm
device tree node of the rev2 DTB (scripts/patch-dts.py).
